      <category>San Francisco</category>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://images.axios.com/LwS4k8WT-bsJgkmLzQyQsCZGk3Q=/0x464:5712x3677/1920x1080/2026/11/05/1793922373001.jpeg?w=3840" alt="High water along the Embarcadero waterfront" style="max-width:100%"/></p>
<p><b>El Niño-driven Kelvin waves can raise coastal water 6 to 12 inches before winter storms even arrive; more extreme tides are expected around Thanksgiving and Christmas.</b></p>
